{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"otelgrpc module stabilization completion date"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"- Robert Pająk\\n\\n- David Ashpole\\n\\n- Mike Blum\\n\\n## Action Items\\n\\n- Robert:\\n\\n  - Work with GC to set up a maintainers mailing list for OSS-Fuzz notifications and ensure appropriate access for Go SIG maintainers.\\n\\n  - Consider manual recreation of older OSS-Fuzz issues if needed; revisit auto GitHub issue filing after triage process matures.\\n\\n  - Take ownership of otelhttp issue [#7254](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254); draft a document clarifying error marking approach and semconv alignment.\\n\\n  - Enable GitHub signature releases for OTel Go; update releasing docs; ensure artifacts are uploaded at release time and signatures published. Reference: [sig-security #164](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164).\\n\\n- Damien:\\n\\n  - Open an issue to kick off an audit of the otelhttp API for stabilization and coordinate reviews.\\n\\n- David (dashpole):\\n\\n  - Monitor semconv RPC stabilization efforts; once stable, drive otelgrpc module stabilization.\\n\\n  - Sync with Josh regarding gRPC team engagement; explore KubeCon conversations if feasible.\\n\\n- Mike:\\n\\n  - Iterate on the otel Explorer Go docs schema:\\n\\n    - Align with OTEL semantic conventions.\\n\\n    - Ensure Weaver compatibility.\\n\\n    - Provide a JSON Schema (or CUE) for validation.\\n\\n    - Consider linking instrumentations to existing semconv references.\\n\\n- Tyler:\\n\\n  - Assign relevant GitHub tasks/issues from this meeting.\\n\\n  - Confirm KubeCon schedule and cancel the Zoom SIG meeting during KubeCon week; share booth details with the community.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"robert paj ą k david ashpol mike blum action item robert work with gc to set up a maintain mail list for os fuzz notif and ensur appropri access for go sig maintain consid manual recreat of older os fuzz issu if need revisit auto github issu file after triag process matur take ownership of otelhttp issu 7254 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 draft a document clarifi error mark approach and semconv align enabl github signatur releas for otel go updat releas doc ensur artifact are upload at releas time and signatur publish refer sig secur 164 http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 damien open an issu to kick off an audit of the otelhttp api for stabil and coordin review david dashpol monitor semconv rpc stabil effort onc stabl drive otelgrpc modul stabil sync with josh regard grpc team engag explor kubecon convers if feasibl mike iter on the otel explor go doc schema align with otel semant convent ensur weaver compat provid a json schema or cue for valid consid link instrument to exist semconv refer tyler assign relev github task issu from this meet confirm kubecon schedul and cancel the zoom sig meet dure kubecon week share booth detail with the communiti\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"21d887bde8f8d5d9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4416609838518518, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.33333333407407406, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6944255, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-06]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479655348  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:39:04Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:40:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-30\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n- Damien Mathieu\\n\\n- Robert Pająk\\n\\n- David Ashpole\\n\\n- Mike Blum\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### Monitoring bugs reported by OSS-Fuzz\\n\\n- David proposed enabling automatic filing of OSS-Fuzz findings as GitHub issues to track and triage them in-repo.\\n\\n- Robert noted OSS-Fuzz runs in Google CI; access and notifications currently limited. Some maintainers may need to be added as contacts.\\n\\n- Tyler and David highlighted that OSS-Fuzz does not file public issues by default due to potential security sensitivity of fuzz findings.\\n\\n- Consensus:\\n\\n  - Start by setting up a maintainers mailing list for OSS-Fuzz notifications (via GC) and trial monitoring for a few months.\\n\\n  - Avoid enabling public GitHub issue filing for now; reassess after triage/verification workflows are in place.\\n\\n  - Robert can manually recreate older issues if needed.\\n\\n- Bryan shared Prometheus project’s recent discussion comparing OSS-Fuzz with Go’s built-in fuzzing; Robert emphasized OSS-Fuzz’s continuous background fuzzing as a benefit.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [Monitoring bugs reported by OSS Fuzz #7549](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/7549)\\n\\n### Stabilization of otelgrpc\\n\\n- Community request to stabilize otelgrpc noted by Tyler.\\n\\n- Blockers:\\n\\n  - Stabilization of RPC semantic conventions (semconv) must come first.\\n\\n  - Audit of the current otelgrpc API to remove cruft and confirm stability.\\n\\n- Damien clarified that stabilization does not imply restoring the old interceptor—it should remain removed.\\n\\n- David is willing to drive module stability once semconv stabilizes; however, gRPC engagement has been sporadic and driven by their internal roadmap.\\n\\n- Strategy discussion:\\n\\n  - OTel could continue owning and maintaining a gRPC instrumentation package, with the option to deprecate later if gRPC ships native instrumentation aligned with semconv.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 06 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479655348 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 39 04z updat 2025 11 03t09 40 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 30 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham damien mathieu robert paj ą k david ashpol mike blum transcript monitor bug report by os fuzz david propos enabl automat file of os fuzz find a github issu to track and triag them in repo robert note os fuzz run in googl ci access and notif current limit some maintain may need to be ad a contact tyler and david highlight that os fuzz doe not file public issu by default due to potenti secur sensit of fuzz find consensus start by set up a maintain mail list for os fuzz notif via gc and trial monitor for a few month avoid enabl public github issu file for now reassess after triag verif workflow are in place robert can manual recreat older issu if need bryan share prometheus project s recent discuss compar os fuzz with go s built in fuzz robert emphas os fuzz s continu background fuzz a a benefit refer monitor bug report by os fuzz 7549 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 7549 stabil of otelgrpc communiti request to stabil otelgrpc note by tyler blocker stabil of rpc semant convent semconv must come first audit of the current otelgrpc api to remov cruft and confirm stabil damien clarifi that stabil doe not impli restor the old interceptor it should remain remov david is will to drive modul stabil onc semconv stabil howev grpc engag ha been sporad and driven by their intern roadmap strategi discuss otel could continu own and maintain a grpc instrument packag with the option to deprec later if grpc ship nativ instrument align with semconv\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"37d8c65557d9108d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.42605493795473254, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.29629629707818933, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7288251, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Seek more engagement from gRPC; attempt in-person conversations at KubeCon if possible. David will sync with Josh on outreach.\\n\\n- Conclusion: Not likely to stabilize this year; set a goal to finalize a strategy next year once semconv progress is clearer.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [Stabilization of otelgrpc](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8078)?\\n\\n  - Related: [https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/8265](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/8265)  \\n\\n  - We need the semconv to stabilize  \\n\\n  - There needs to be involvement from gRPC to progress this  \\n\\n  - [David] Update: I’m told that the SIG is active and is working towards stabilization. Not sure if gRPC is involved.  \\n\\n### Stabilization of otelhttp\\n\\n- Damien proposed starting an API audit for otelhttp to move towards stabilization.\\n\\n- A known bug (issue #7254) may be the only blocker; it’s a behavioral change around how errors are marked (events vs attributes) and interacts with semconv/spec wording.\\n\\n- Agreement:\\n\\n  - Begin the API review.\\n\\n  - Robert will take ownership of #7254 and draft a document clarifying interpretation and proposed resolution.\\n\\n  - The existence of bugs does not inherently block stabilization; they can be fixed post-stabilization if changes are non-breaking or properly versioned.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- Blocker (only one I think): [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254)  \\n\\n### OTel Explorer Go docs\\n\\n- Mike outlined a project to revamp the OTEL registry/explorer with a schema that documents spans/metrics emitted by instrumentations, aiming to render via Hugo and enable static analysis across Go SDKs and contrib modules.\\n\\n- Tyler’s feedback:\\n\\n  - Strong requirement: align schema with semantic conventions and ensure it’s compatible with Weaver (to enable validation and transformations across versions).\\n\\n  - Consider providing a JSON Schema (or CUE) for validation and potentially linking to existing semconv definitions to keep the spec concise.\\n\\n  - Scope can include eBPF/auto-instrumentation; representation should still fit the schema as long as it maps to OTEL signals.\\n\\n- Mike will iterate on the schema, explore Weaver integration, and coordinate with SIGs as needed.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n  - Context: [https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000](https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000)  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"seek more engag from grpc attempt in person convers at kubecon if possibl david will sync with josh on outreach conclus not like to stabil this year set a goal to final a strategi next year onc semconv progress is clearer refer stabil of otelgrpc http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8078 relat http github com grpc grpc go issu 8265 http github com grpc grpc go issu 8265 we need the semconv to stabil there need to be involv from grpc to progress this david updat i m told that the sig is activ and is work toward stabil not sure if grpc is involv stabil of otelhttp damien propos start an api audit for otelhttp to move toward stabil a known bug issu 7254 may be the onli blocker it s a behavior chang around how error are mark event v attribut and interact with semconv spec word agreement begin the api review robert will take ownership of 7254 and draft a document clarifi interpret and propos resolut the exist of bug doe not inher block stabil they can be fix post stabil if chang are non break or proper version refer blocker onli one i think http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 otel explor go doc mike outlin a project to revamp the otel registri explor with a schema that document span metric emit by instrument aim to render via hugo and enabl static analysi across go sdks and contrib modul tyler s feedback strong requir align schema with semant convent and ensur it s compat with weaver to enabl valid and transform across version consid provid a json schema or cue for valid and potenti link to exist semconv definit to keep the spec concis scope can includ ebpf auto instrument represent should still fit the schema a long a it map to otel signal mike will iter on the schema explor weaver integr and coordin with sig a need refer context http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"5449cc5184194ce6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3714909781604938, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.22222222308641976, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71978474, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-06]\\n\\n# Issue: Restore deprecated `UnaryClientInterceptor` to maintain backwards compatibility (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8078)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8078  \\n\\n**Author**: nicholasngai  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-27T23:28:07Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-31T09:47:48Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (not_planned)  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nSignal boosting [this comment](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7104#issuecomment-3412968109):\\n\\nHey folks! Can we revisit the decision to remove `UnaryClientInterceptor` and friends from this library? Is there any security issue with leaving that API in?\\n\\nI understand Otel is still in an unstable version, but this change means we are no longer able to upgrade otelgrpc to the latest version anymore. We have a pretty big chain of dependencies internally depending on otel and bumping all of them is not a simple matter. We won’t be able to upgrade otelgrpc until the entire dependency chain which spans across multiple orgs and third-party libraries is up to date.\\n\\nIs it possible to avoid breaking changes to the API surface even if the module counts as unstable?\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-06]\\n\\n# Issue: Restore deprecated `UnaryClientInterceptor` to maintain backwards compatibility (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8078)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8078  \\n\\n**Author**: nicholasngai  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-27T23:28:07Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-31T09:47:48Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (not_planned)  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (11)\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-28T08:36:24Z\\n\\ncc @dashpole as code owner.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dashpole** — 2025-10-28T20:02:57Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 06 issu restor deprec unaryclientinterceptor to maintain backward compat open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8078 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8078 author nicholasngai creat 2025 10 27t23 28 07z updat 2025 10 31t09 47 48z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close not _ plan label mileston descript signal boost this comment http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7104 issuecom 3412968109 hey folk can we revisit the decis to remov unaryclientinterceptor and friend from this librari is there ani secur issu with leav that api in i understand otel is still in an unstabl version but this chang mean we are no longer abl to upgrad otelgrpc to the latest version anymor we have a pretti big chain of depend intern depend on otel and bump all of them is not a simpl matter we won t be abl to upgrad otelgrpc until the entir depend chain which span across multipl org and third parti librari is up to date is it possibl to avoid break chang to the api surfac even if the modul count a unstabl sourc id src issu 06 issu restor deprec unaryclientinterceptor to maintain backward compat open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8078 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8078 author nicholasngai creat 2025 10 27t23 28 07z updat 2025 10 31t09 47 48z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close not _ plan label mileston discuss 11 dmathieu 2025 10 28t08 36 24z cc dashpol a code owner dashpol 2025 10 28t20 02 57z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"id\": \"f9941ae79d02a91d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3648550141604938, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.22222222308641976, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69766486, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4910, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:12\", \"token_count\": 1517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Can you share more about why you aren't able to migrate to the stats handler?  We [deprecated](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/4534) the interceptors almost 2 years ago, which seems like plenty of time to migrate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-28T20:40:37Z\\n\\nEven if we removed all of our references, references in transitive dependencies still cause compilation errors, and we don’t have control over the timeline at which transitive dependencies remove those code references.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-29T08:35:31Z\\n\\nThat doesn't look like a good reason to me. There will always be unmaintained transitive dependencies that prevent this kind of upgrades.\\n\\nThat's tech debt that needs to be fixed, not kept on our end.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T16:28:55Z\\n\\nThe question is really whether we can rely on otelgrpc to be stable! For now, we are stuck on v0.58.0 because of compilation errors on higher versions introduced by the breaking change. If there is an urgent security patch introduced, we won’t be able to upgrade to it.\\n\\nGenerally, with Golang, we avoid breaking changes aggressively avoid these kinds of things. Does maintaining this interceptor involve significant overhead from the maintainers?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T17:37:26Z\\n\\nPlease do not rely on an unstable package as being stable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T17:38:42Z\\n\\nAre there plans to make this package stable? Or are we sticking with [ZeroVer](https://0ver.org/) for the forseeable future?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T18:06:47Z\\n\\n> Are there plans to make this package stable?\\n\\nThere is definitely desire among project contributor to progress this package towards stability. But please understand this is an open-source project. It is driven by a the dedicated effort of engineers who donate their time to working on this. That time is valuable and allocated to many efforts.\\n\\nI'm happy to add the question of stabilization to our weekly SIG meeting happening tomorrow. @nicholasngai I would strongly suggest you attend the meeting tomorrow to discuss your use-case and help motivate allocation of effort for this stabilization. I don't anticipate this stabilization happening within 2025, but I could see us prioritizing it for 2026 if we have community involvement and/or added developer help here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"can you share more about whi you aren t abl to migrat to the stat handler we deprec http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 4534 the interceptor almost 2 year ago which seem like plenti of time to migrat nicholasngai 2025 10 28t20 40 37z even if we remov all of our refer refer in transit depend still caus compil error and we don t have control over the timelin at which transit depend remov those code refer dmathieu 2025 10 29t08 35 31z that doesn t look like a good reason to me there will alway be unmaintain transit depend that prevent this kind of upgrad that s tech debt that need to be fix not kept on our end nicholasngai 2025 10 29t16 28 55z the question is realli whether we can reli on otelgrpc to be stabl for now we are stuck on v0 580 becaus of compil error on higher version introduc by the break chang if there is an urgent secur patch introduc we won t be abl to upgrad to it general with golang we avoid break chang aggress avoid these kind of thing doe maintain this interceptor involv signific overhead from the maintain mralia 2025 10 29t17 37 26z pleas do not reli on an unstabl packag a be stabl nicholasngai 2025 10 29t17 38 42z are there plan to make this packag stabl or are we stick with zerov http 0ver org for the forseeabl futur mralia 2025 10 29t18 06 47z are there plan to make this packag stabl there is definit desir among project contributor to progress this packag toward stabil but pleas understand this is an open sourc project it is driven by a the dedic effort of engin who donat their time to work on this that time is valuabl and alloc to mani effort i m happi to add the question of stabil to our week sig meet happen tomorrow nicholasngai i would strong suggest you attend the meet tomorrow to discus your use case and help motiv alloc of effort for this stabil i don t anticip this stabil happen within 2025 but i could see u priorit it for 2026 if we have communiti involv and or ad develop help here\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"id\": \"1afc8125e2debda9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32333218636625516, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1481481490946502, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73209494, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4910, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:12\", \"token_count\": 1517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**dashpole** — 2025-10-29T18:51:27Z\\n\\nIt is also worth calling out that we depend on telemetry naming conventions, which are still unstable for gRPC, and prevent us from making the module stable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-30T08:46:26Z\\n\\notelgrpc being unstable, it's kinda as if we were starting from scratch today. If that were the case, we wouldn't implement something that is deprecated in the underlying API, that makes no sense.\\n\\nEven if we make the package stable today, we still wouldn't implement something that is deprecated. The only case where we'd keep deprecated code is if we were stable and needed to keep backwards compatibility.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-31T09:47:48Z\\n\\nClosing, as based on yesterday's discussions during the SIG meeting, we have agreement that we won't bring back the interceptor.\\n\\nNote that nothing prevents you from copying the code as it was before and setting up your own internal module.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-06]\\n\\n# Issue: Restore deprecated `UnaryClientInterceptor` to maintain backwards compatibility (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8078)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8078  \\n\\n**Author**: nicholasngai  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-27T23:28:07Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-31T09:47:48Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (not_planned)  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2025-10-31T09:47:48Z · **closed** by dmathieu\\n\\n- 2025-11-03T09:39:05Z · **cross-referenced** by pellared ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"dashpol 2025 10 29t18 51 27z it is also worth call out that we depend on telemetri name convent which are still unstabl for grpc and prevent u from make the modul stabl dmathieu 2025 10 30t08 46 26z otelgrpc be unstabl it s kinda a if we were start from scratch today if that were the case we wouldn t implement someth that is deprec in the under api that make no sens even if we make the packag stabl today we still wouldn t implement someth that is deprec the onli case where we d keep deprec code is if we were stabl and need to keep backward compat dmathieu 2025 10 31t09 47 48z close a base on yesterday s discuss dure the sig meet we have agreement that we won t bring back the interceptor note that noth prevent you from copi the code a it wa befor and set up your own intern modul sourc id src issu 06 issu restor deprec unaryclientinterceptor to maintain backward compat open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8078 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8078 author nicholasngai creat 2025 10 27t23 28 07z updat 2025 10 31t09 47 48z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close not _ plan label mileston timelin 2025 10 31t09 47 48z close by dmathieu 2025 11 03t09 39 05z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"id\": \"458f8eef1f171cca\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32085213436625515, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1481481490946502, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7238281, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4910, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:12\", \"token_count\": 1517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Attendees\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn  \\n\\n- Owen Williams  \\n\\n- Sam Xie\\n\\n- Alex Boten  \\n\\n- David Ashpole  \\n\\n- Bryan Boreham  \\n\\n- (Mentioned: Robert Pająk)\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Discussions\\n\\n### 1. Next Go release & OTelConf RC support\\n\\n- Release blocked on RC support module; PR needs reviews.\\n\\n- Requested changes from Alex do not need to be in the current PR.\\n\\n- Module is `0.x`; breaking changes acceptable later.\\n\\n- Avoid exposing public API known to be removed immediately.\\n\\n- Discussed handling experimental features:\\n\\n  - `WithExperimentalFeatures`-style flag likely unhelpful.\\n\\n  - Possible `x` submodule to clearly isolate experimental APIs.\\n\\n  - Aligns with OTel-wide push for opt-in experimental features.\\n\\n### 2. HTTP default client deprecation (OTel HTTP)\\n\\n- Work deprecating default HTTP client usage is in progress.\\n\\n- `POST`/`GET` helpers rely on `http.DefaultClient` and limit configurability.\\n\\n- Follow-up PRs exist; need review for inclusion in upcoming release.\\n\\n### 3. Observability work & non-blocking PRs\\n\\n- Several observability PRs (e.g., self-observability for OTel gRPC) are ongoing, not release-blocking.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 attende tyler yahn o