 \"token_count\": 1379, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Two non-observability items noted:\\n\\n  - Sync map / atomics for fixed bucket histograms.\\n\\n  - Exemplar reservoir changes.\\n\\n- Safe to slip to next release; include if ready.\\n\\n### 4. Stabilizing new attribute value types\\n\\n- Discussion about stabilizing new spec attribute types (byte arrays, “any” type).\\n\\n- Prototype implementation exists and needs review.\\n\\n- Considered tricky; careful review needed around limits and types.\\n\\n### 5. Processor `Enabled` method\\n\\n- Proposal from Robert to move `Enabled` from filter processor to main processor interface.\\n\\n- Spec now stabilized and allows this.\\n\\n- Pros: consistent API, less ad-hoc type assertion/boilerplate in docs.\\n\\n- Con: processors that are “always enabled” need a trivial `Enabled() bool { return true }`.\\n\\n- General agreement; will revisit for final confirmation.\\n\\n### 6. OTLP `insecure` support (logs, env vars, spec)\\n\\n- PR adds `insecure` (env var) support for OTLP **logs**, matching traces/metrics.\\n\\n- HTTP OTLP config historically messy; env vars common in practice.\\n\\n- Spec unclear due to moratorium on env vars.\\n\\n- Direction: add logs support in Go; push for spec clarity later.\\n\\n### 7. Collector protobuf changes & PDataGen\\n\\n- Collector removed dependency on Go protobuf types; now uses `pdataGen`.\\n\\n- Large internal rewrite; significant line count reduction.\\n\\n- Benchmarks improved (fewer allocations).\\n\\n- Some cross-language quirks surfaced but manageable.\\n\\n- Go SIG interested in exploring similar approaches; needs more benchmarking.\\n\\n### 8. KubeCon & talks\\n\\n- First SIG meeting since KubeCon.\\n\\n- Members encouraged to share notable talks and videos once available.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- Merge OTelConf RC support PR as-is (pending normal review).\\n\\n- Track experimental API structure review (e.g., `x` submodule) under the `1.40.0` milestone.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"two non observ item note sync map atom for fix bucket histogram exemplar reservoir chang safe to slip to next releas includ if readi 4 stabil new attribut valu type discuss about stabil new spec attribut type byte array ani type prototyp implement exist and need review consid tricki care review need around limit and type 5 processor enabl method propos from robert to move enabl from filter processor to main processor interfac spec now stabil and allow this pro consist api less ad hoc type assert boilerpl in doc con processor that are alway enabl need a trivial enabl bool return true general agreement will revisit for final confirm 6 otlp insecur support log env var spec pr add insecur env var support for otlp log match trace metric http otlp config histor messi env var common in practic spec unclear due to moratorium on env var direct add log support in go push for spec clariti later 7 collector protobuf chang pdatagen collector remov depend on go protobuf type now us pdatagen larg intern rewrit signific line count reduct benchmark improv fewer alloc some cross languag quirk surfac but manag go sig interest in explor similar approach need more benchmark 8 kubecon talk first sig meet sinc kubecon member encourag to share notabl talk and video onc avail sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 decis merg otelconf rc support pr ais pend normal review track experiment api structur review e g x submodul under the 140 0 mileston\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874202ba8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"id\": \"2174523acdce943d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3143340343662552, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1481481490946502, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7021011, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874202ba8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3959, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 1379, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### PR status: JSON/YAML unmarshalling\\n\\n- A small change (error tag) was suggested and applied.\\n\\n- Build is running; plan is to merge once green.\\n\\n### Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE\\n\\nReference: Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059\\n\\n- Goal:\\n\\n  - If the env var is present, load the indicated config file and configure the SDK automatically, minimizing user code.\\n\\n- Current ecosystem notes:\\n\\n  - PHP reports support; other languages vary (JS likely working on it; C++ explicitly not supporting).\\n\\n  - Go users are accustomed to programmatic setup; unclear if SDK-level support is necessary.\\n\\n- Go implementation options discussed:\\n\\n  - SDK experimental feature-flag approach:\\n\\n    - Use internal “x”/experimental packages to expose a feature gate for the env var.\\n\\n    - Check the env var during SDK setup (e.g., TracerProvider construction), and if enabled, configure from the file.\\n\\n    - Complications:\\n\\n      - Potential import cycles (e.g., if otelconf needs sdk and vice versa).\\n\\n      - Decision required on how to handle passed options vs. config file (ignore vs. merge).\\n\\n      - Requires similar work across trace, metrics, and logs modules.\\n\\n  - Contrib-first approach (preferred short term):\\n\\n    - Implement in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf:\\n\\n      - Provide an explicit function to load from OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE and construct/return SDK providers.\\n\\n      - Optionally offer an init-based side effect that sets the global provider if the env var is set (not ideal, but acceptable during experimental phase to collect feedback).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol transcript pr status json yaml unmarshal a small chang error tag wa suggest and appli build is run plan is to merg onc green ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file refer ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 goal if the env var is present load the indic config file and configur the sdk automat minim user code current ecosystem note php report support other languag vari j like work on it c explicit not support go user are accustom to programmat setup unclear if sdk level support is necessari go implement option discuss sdk experiment featur flag approach use intern x experiment packag to expos a featur gate for the env var check the env var dure sdk setup e g tracerprovid construct and if enabl configur from the file complic potenti import cycl e g if otelconf need sdk and vice versa decis requir on how to handl pass option v config file ignor v merg requir similar work across trace metric and log modul contrib first approach prefer short term implement in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf provid an explicit function to load from otel _ experiment _ config _ file and construct return sdk provid option offer an init base side effect that set the global provid if the env var is set not ideal but accept dure experiment phase to collect feedback\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1fe86388dce9138e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30823338436625514, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1481481490946502, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6817656, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\":